{
  "title": "IT Faculty Overseas Leave",
  "prompt": "Any undergraduate student of the Faculty of Information Technology who intends to travel overseas during the academic term must obtain prior approval before leaving the country. The student submits a request stating their full name, index number, the destination country, the departure date, the return date, and the reason for the trip. The request first goes to the student's Academic Advisor for approval. Once the Academic Advisor approves, it goes to the Head of the Department of Information Technology. At any point an approver may either approve the request, reject it with a reason, or ask the student for more information, in which case the student is asked for the missing detail and the request returns to that same approver. If the total duration of the trip exceeds 30 days, the request must additionally be endorsed by the Dean of the Faculty after the Head of Department has approved. When all required approvals are complete, the student is issued a signed overseas leave authorization letter and notified that it is ready for collection."
}

